WEBVTT

00:02.435 --> 00:04.164
Yo, dude. What up?

00:06.005 --> 00:07.063
Just follow my lead.

00:08.341 --> 00:10.206
Oh, this is awesome.

00:10.376 --> 00:14.904
Eh. It's just a little surf shack
where I keep my board, beer and brother.

00:17.050 --> 00:18.847
How are they breaking today, broheim?

00:20.987 --> 00:22.352
How are what breaking?

00:22.922 --> 00:26.358
- Dude smokes way too much weed.
- Oh.

00:26.860 --> 00:28.919
The waves, Poindexter.

00:29.095 --> 00:33.259
Oh. Oh, the waves. The, uh...
The waves are...

00:34.134 --> 00:35.624
...gnarly?

00:36.970 --> 00:38.267
All right. Let's hit it.

00:39.139 --> 00:41.369
Oh, I intend to.

00:42.976 --> 00:44.944
Why don't you head out?
I'll throw on my suit and meet you.

00:45.345 --> 00:46.972
Awesome.

00:49.849 --> 00:53.250
Mm. Bodacious and tubular.

00:55.388 --> 00:58.221
Uh, excuse me, Moondoggie.

00:58.391 --> 01:00.052
- Quick question.
Yeah.

01:00.226 --> 01:01.716
You don't surf, do you?

01:01.895 --> 01:03.487
Not a bit.

01:03.663 --> 01:07.064
So how did Gidget get the idea
you were the Big Kahuna?

01:07.367 --> 01:09.927
I told her I hang ten
and I guess she misunderstood.

01:11.404 --> 01:13.235
You're going to hell, you know.

01:13.406 --> 01:16.807
I don't think so. I believe
in a loving God who forgives little fibs...

01:16.976 --> 01:19.308
...as long as they lead
to recreational sex.

01:20.213 --> 01:22.147
You really wanna drag God into this?

01:22.315 --> 01:24.875
Who gave me the penis, Alan?

01:26.519 --> 01:28.248
Since when do you have a wet suit?

01:28.421 --> 01:33.051
Since I moved to the beach
and noticed it was full of hot surfer chicks.

01:35.728 --> 01:40.461
If I lived next to Jellystone Park
I'd have a bear suit and a picnic basket.

01:42.535 --> 01:44.264
Would you get the door?

01:48.374 --> 01:49.773
Oopsie.

01:49.943 --> 01:53.674
Smooth. So just out of curiosity...

01:54.480 --> 01:56.471
...how exactly do you plan
to pull this off?

01:56.649 --> 01:58.173
Simple.

01:58.384 --> 02:01.046
Paddle out, yell shark and paddle in.

02:01.221 --> 02:03.451
- So you've thought this through?
- I'm not an idiot, Alan.

02:08.161 --> 02:09.423
Oopsie.

02:11.431 --> 02:12.989
Over here.

02:13.166 --> 02:14.565
Careful.

02:14.734 --> 02:16.201
What happened?

02:16.369 --> 02:19.065
I don't know,
this tiny wave came at us...

02:19.239 --> 02:22.970
...I let it go, he screamed like a girl
and fell off his board.

02:23.543 --> 02:26.535
I had to give him mouth-to-mouth.
He swallowed a lot of water.

02:27.280 --> 02:28.611
He's gonna be okay?

02:28.781 --> 02:31.978
I think so.
He tried slipping me the tongue.

02:32.752 --> 02:34.811
Charlie, can you hear me?

02:37.056 --> 02:38.580
Sha...

02:38.758 --> 02:41.318
- What?
- Sha...

02:41.494 --> 02:43.257
I think he's trying to say "shark. "

02:56.776 --> 02:58.971
- Want something to drink?
- Oh.

02:59.145 --> 03:00.578
Yeah.

03:04.017 --> 03:05.143
Ugh.

03:07.153 --> 03:09.121
- What is this?
- Water.

03:09.489 --> 03:11.719
Are you crazy?
I almost drowned in that stuff.

03:17.196 --> 03:18.595
Where's my little hard body?

03:18.898 --> 03:21.264
He took off with that girl
you brought home.

03:24.237 --> 03:26.603
Other than that,
your plan worked like a charm.

03:26.773 --> 03:31.073
Fine, go ahead and mock me,
but I could've died out there.

03:31.244 --> 03:34.042
Well, the sea is a harsh mistress...

03:34.514 --> 03:36.744
...and you're a moron.

03:38.651 --> 03:41.017
What? You said to mock you.

03:41.187 --> 03:43.121
- It's no joke, Alan.
- Oh, come on.

03:43.289 --> 03:45.849
You tried to scam your way
into a surf bunny's shorts...

03:46.025 --> 03:48.858
...and ended up French kissing
a handsome young lifeguard.

03:49.896 --> 03:51.090
How is that not a joke?

03:53.199 --> 03:55.292
It's not a joke because...

03:57.170 --> 04:00.435
...something happened out there
while I was drowning.

04:00.606 --> 04:04.770
What, did your entire sordid,
degenerate life flash before your eyes?

04:04.944 --> 04:06.571
I wish.

04:08.381 --> 04:11.077
No, no, no. It was...

04:11.451 --> 04:12.816
Ah, you're not gonna believe me.

04:13.419 --> 04:14.443
Try me.

04:16.856 --> 04:18.289
I saw Dad.

04:18.458 --> 04:20.119
Oh, baloney.

04:21.260 --> 04:22.921
You know what? Just forget it.

04:23.096 --> 04:25.587
Oh, come on,
it was probably just a hallucination...

04:25.765 --> 04:28.529
...caused by, you know,
brain cells dying.

04:30.603 --> 04:32.867
No, I'm used to that.

04:34.507 --> 04:37.135
This was no hallucination.

04:37.310 --> 04:39.574
Dad was right there in the water
with me.

04:40.013 --> 04:41.844
All right, for the sake of argument...

04:42.015 --> 04:45.246
...let's assume that you saw the spirit
of our dead father.

04:45.418 --> 04:48.717
What did he do, reach a hand out
to guide you to the great beyond?

04:48.888 --> 04:51.254
Don't be ridiculous.

04:52.058 --> 04:54.390
He didn't have hands.

04:55.595 --> 04:59.224
It was just his head
kind of floating there...

04:59.399 --> 05:03.358
...like the great and powerful oz.

05:05.038 --> 05:07.404
Or one of the Pep Boys.

05:09.042 --> 05:10.236
Wow.

05:10.777 --> 05:12.210
Manny, Moe or Jack?

05:12.378 --> 05:13.902
Jack.

05:17.383 --> 05:18.714
And he spoke to me.

05:18.885 --> 05:21.752
Oh. Oh. You were able
to hear him underwater?

05:21.921 --> 05:22.945
How weird.

05:23.122 --> 05:25.283
Oh, that's the part that bumps you?

05:26.059 --> 05:29.153
You were able to hear him
because you were imagining it.

05:29.328 --> 05:31.888
- It was in your head.
- No. Oh, no.

05:32.065 --> 05:35.592
In a million years, my mind could not
have made up what he said to me.

05:35.768 --> 05:36.860
What did he say?

05:38.504 --> 05:41.098
Something that made my blood run cold.

05:41.808 --> 05:43.241
What?

05:44.911 --> 05:47.209
- Never mind, I probably heard him wrong.
- Charlie.

05:47.380 --> 05:49.041
Please don't make me say it.

05:49.215 --> 05:51.149
Come on, Charlie, I am your brother.

05:51.317 --> 05:53.751
Whatever it was,
we'll deal with it together.

05:56.489 --> 05:58.218
He said:

05:58.391 --> 06:00.882
"Take care of your mother. "

06:06.866 --> 06:08.094
Well, good luck with that.

06:14.907 --> 06:17.068
- Hey.
- Hey.

06:17.577 --> 06:19.477
Dad said you almost drowned today.

06:20.279 --> 06:22.839
- Yep.
- Are you okay now?

06:23.382 --> 06:24.747
I'm fine.

06:25.051 --> 06:26.279
Can I ask you a question?

06:26.953 --> 06:29.922
- Sure.
- It's about what happens when you die.

06:30.423 --> 06:31.447
Okay.

06:31.891 --> 06:33.620
Who gets your car?

06:36.529 --> 06:38.087
Go away.

06:39.065 --> 06:41.693
You're right. Not a good time to ask.

06:43.336 --> 06:44.963
So...

06:45.138 --> 06:46.730
...what are you doing?

06:47.740 --> 06:49.731
Thinking about Dad.

06:50.042 --> 06:52.306
Yeah, about that.

06:52.478 --> 06:55.208
I was wondering, when you saw him...

06:55.381 --> 07:00.114
...assuming you saw him,
did he ask about me?

07:01.287 --> 07:04.723
No, he just said,
"Take care of your mother. "

07:05.057 --> 07:06.046
Huh.

07:06.225 --> 07:07.886
Didrt mention me at all?

07:08.060 --> 07:09.118
Nope.

07:09.295 --> 07:10.887
Typical.

07:12.198 --> 07:13.222
Oh, here we go.

07:13.399 --> 07:15.867
I'm saying, the guy
doesn't get in touch for 30 years.

07:16.035 --> 07:18.731
It wouldn't kill him to throw in a quick,
"Hello, Alan. "

07:19.172 --> 07:21.470
Dead or alive, that's just rude.

07:21.641 --> 07:24.007
Tell you what,
why don't you go fill up the tub...

07:24.177 --> 07:26.270
...I'll hold your head under the water
until the bubbles stop...

07:26.445 --> 07:28.845
...and then you can tell him
how offended you are.

07:29.715 --> 07:32.479
Oh, no.
I have nothing to say to him now.

07:36.489 --> 07:39.219
How does he expect me
to take care of her?

07:39.392 --> 07:42.327
I don't know. Why don't you try
treating her like a human being?

07:43.696 --> 07:45.789
No, that can't be it.

07:46.332 --> 07:48.596
What if I put her
in an assisted living facility?

07:49.302 --> 07:51.167
That's ridiculous.
She's a healthy woman.

07:51.337 --> 07:53.805
I'm not saying
she wouldn't put up a fight.

07:53.973 --> 07:56.237
But, hey, crumble up
a few Xanax in her mimosa...

07:56.409 --> 07:59.503
...and we could probably coax her
into a cave full of bats.

08:00.746 --> 08:03.010
I don't think that's what Dad meant.

08:03.182 --> 08:05.013
How do you know? Did he talk to you?

08:05.184 --> 08:07.209
No. He talked to me.

08:07.753 --> 08:10.051
Sure, rub my nose in it.

08:10.223 --> 08:11.349
How about this?

08:11.524 --> 08:14.516
When was the last time you called her
to see how she was doing?

08:15.294 --> 08:16.659
Uh... ooh.

08:16.829 --> 08:18.353
- What's today? Sunday?
- Mm.

08:18.531 --> 08:20.021
Then never.

08:20.866 --> 08:22.891
Why don't you start with that?

08:24.437 --> 08:26.905
Okay, fine.

08:27.073 --> 08:28.631
Remember her number?

08:28.808 --> 08:30.241
I've got it on speed dial.

08:30.776 --> 08:33.301
Six, six, six.

08:33.479 --> 08:35.037
Cute, huh?

08:37.783 --> 08:39.683
Hey, Mom. It's Charlie.

08:39.986 --> 08:43.547
Nothing's the matter,
I just called to see how you're doing.

08:43.889 --> 08:45.322
No, I'm not drunk.

08:45.491 --> 08:48.722
I was just thinking about you
and thought I'd call.

08:49.328 --> 08:51.728
I swear to God I'm not drunk.

08:51.897 --> 08:55.424
Peter Piper picked a peck
of pickled peppers, you happy?

08:56.402 --> 08:57.494
So, what's going on?

08:57.670 --> 08:59.729
I haven't talked to you in a whi...

08:59.905 --> 09:02.840
Well, I'm talking to you now.

09:04.844 --> 09:08.075
Okay. Okay. Okay.

09:08.247 --> 09:10.579
Okay. Excuse me?

09:10.816 --> 09:14.377
Okay. Okay. Okay.

09:14.854 --> 09:16.321
So...

09:16.489 --> 09:18.081
...everything okay?

09:19.759 --> 09:22.091
I'm taking her to lunch tomorrow.

09:22.261 --> 09:23.285
Voluntarily?

09:24.330 --> 09:27.595
Wow, you must have really had
a spiritual experience out there.

09:27.767 --> 09:31.999
Let's face it, Alan,
when Dad was alive, I was a rotten son.

09:32.171 --> 09:33.297
Oh, you sure were.

09:33.472 --> 09:35.406
You were horrible. I remember the time...

09:35.574 --> 09:37.633
The point is...

09:37.810 --> 09:40.643
...maybe I've got a chance
to make up for it now.

09:40.813 --> 09:44.340
He wants me to take care of Mom,
then that's what we're gonna do.

09:44.950 --> 09:48.010
Well, that's ver...
Wait a minute, did you say we?

09:48.688 --> 09:50.622
- I'm not going.
- Fine.

09:50.790 --> 09:54.658
Next time I see our father's floating head,
I'm gonna tell him you refused to help.

09:55.428 --> 09:58.864
"I'm gonna tell him. I'm gonna tell him. "
God, you're such a child.

09:59.031 --> 10:01.397
- So you're coming?
- Yeah.

10:04.036 --> 10:08.370
I can't tell you what a treat it is
to have lunch with my two favorite sons.

10:08.708 --> 10:09.970
You have others?

10:10.743 --> 10:12.233
It's an expression, Charlie.

10:13.312 --> 10:15.405
Although I do sponsor
a little boy in Africa.

10:15.715 --> 10:18.878
- No kidding.
- Oh, yes, little Mabutu.

10:19.885 --> 10:23.514
He's in the middle of a civil war
and I still hear from him more than you.

10:25.024 --> 10:27.652
Alan, tell Mom
what that little rascal Jake's been up to.

10:29.462 --> 10:31.794
He hasn't been up to anything.

10:35.701 --> 10:37.999
Okay. So...

10:40.706 --> 10:42.173
I think I'll go to the bathroom.

10:42.608 --> 10:45.736
- Why?
- What do you mean, why? I have to go.

10:45.911 --> 10:48.209
When was the last time
you had a prostate exam?

10:48.381 --> 10:50.008
It feels like I'm having one now.

10:50.182 --> 10:52.582
I'm just expressing concern
for your health.

10:52.752 --> 10:55.687
- You don't have to get snippy.
- I'm not being snippy.

10:56.021 --> 10:58.114
Is it just me or is he snippy?

10:59.558 --> 11:00.684
Try living with him.

11:01.026 --> 11:02.584
Excuse me.

11:02.762 --> 11:04.127
All right, what's going on?

11:04.463 --> 11:06.055
What makes you think
something's going on?

11:06.732 --> 11:09.530
When one of my sons calls me
for no reason...

11:09.702 --> 11:12.933
...and agrees to take me to lunch,
something heinous is going on.

11:13.105 --> 11:16.734
I took you to lunch two weeks ago
for no reason other than I love you.

11:16.909 --> 11:19.776
Oh, yes, the tacky little chain restaurant
in the valley.

11:19.945 --> 11:22.880
That fish shot out of me
like there was a fire drill.

11:24.517 --> 11:26.883
The point is I love you.

11:27.286 --> 11:30.449
The point is I lost four pounds
in two days.

11:32.191 --> 11:35.354
- Well, you do look thinner.
- It's too late for flattery, darling.

11:35.528 --> 11:37.723
Now, what is going on
with your brother?

11:39.064 --> 11:40.929
I don't think he'd be happy with me
if I told you.

11:41.100 --> 11:43.898
Sweetheart,
you're not his favorite person now.

11:45.538 --> 11:48.302
Okay. Here's the thing:

11:48.774 --> 11:50.799
Charlie almost drowned yesterday.

11:50.976 --> 11:52.034
Oh, dear Lord.

11:52.211 --> 11:55.977
I told him over and over again,
two drinks max in the hot tub.

11:56.682 --> 11:57.808
No, he was surfing.

11:57.983 --> 12:00.076
- In the hot tub?
- In the ocean.

12:00.252 --> 12:01.742
Start again.

12:02.054 --> 12:04.249
He was trying to impress some girl.

12:04.423 --> 12:07.620
Ah. Oh, okay. Like the time
he broke his nose playing tetherball.

12:08.194 --> 12:09.388
Exactly.

12:09.562 --> 12:13.498
Anyway, he was convinced
he was near death...

12:14.500 --> 12:15.762
...and that he saw Dad.

12:16.836 --> 12:18.326
He saw your father?

12:19.805 --> 12:21.238
Wow.

12:22.208 --> 12:23.436
How'd he look?

12:23.943 --> 12:25.808
Uh, he was just
kind of a floating head.

12:25.978 --> 12:28.344
Yeah, that's pretty much
how I remember him.

12:28.514 --> 12:30.778
Fairly useless from the neck down.

12:30.950 --> 12:35.182
Anyway, Dad told Charlie
to take care of you.

12:37.656 --> 12:39.317
Really?

12:40.893 --> 12:42.827
- Anything else?
- Nope, that's it.

12:42.995 --> 12:46.795
Just for him to take care of you.
It's like I might as well not even exist.

12:46.966 --> 12:49.434
Oh, Alan, you can't take that personally.

12:49.602 --> 12:52.162
First of all, Charlie was a planned baby.

12:53.205 --> 12:54.729
What was I?

12:54.907 --> 12:58.673
Well, dear, you were a pitcher of margaritas
and a gas station condom.

13:02.348 --> 13:05.840
I had a nice, solid stream of urine,
thank you very much.

13:06.519 --> 13:09.181
- What?
- My prostate is fine.

13:09.355 --> 13:10.845
What kind of table talk is that?

13:11.490 --> 13:12.684
You brought it up.

13:12.858 --> 13:15.986
Doesrt matter who brought it up.
I don't wanna hear about it when I'm eating.

13:17.496 --> 13:19.896
You know what?
This lunch was a bad idea.

13:20.065 --> 13:23.000
Oh, no, don't say that, darling,
it was a wonderful idea.

13:23.168 --> 13:25.568
If I'm being ungracious, I apologize.

13:25.738 --> 13:30.334
All right, let's call it ungracious.
Though we all know what we're thinking.

13:31.810 --> 13:35.678
I guess I'm just a little edgy
because, well...

13:38.284 --> 13:40.013
- Never mind.
- What?

13:40.185 --> 13:42.915
Forget it. My problems are my problems.

13:43.088 --> 13:47.024
I don't expect you to take care of me.

13:49.795 --> 13:55.791
Mom, just for the sake of argument,
let's say that I wanted to take care of you.

13:55.968 --> 13:58.664
- What's going on?
- Nothing.

13:58.837 --> 14:01.567
I'm just having
a little minor surgery tomorrow.

14:01.740 --> 14:04.140
- What kind of surgery?
- It's a woman thing.

14:04.310 --> 14:05.436
Anything I can do?

14:06.178 --> 14:08.146
Just keep me in your prayers.

14:09.448 --> 14:14.249
No, no, no. I will drive you there and then
take you to my place so you can recuperate.

14:14.420 --> 14:18.379
Oh, sweetheart, that's very generous,
but I don't want to be a burden.

14:18.557 --> 14:19.888
Mom, please.

14:20.059 --> 14:22.220
That ship has sailed.

14:23.262 --> 14:25.787
Well, then I accept.

14:25.965 --> 14:26.989
Thank you.

14:31.303 --> 14:33.897
Who buys condoms at a gas station?

14:41.580 --> 14:43.707
Watch your step here.

14:53.425 --> 14:55.552
Thank you, darling.

15:02.635 --> 15:06.662
- What happened to your mouth?
- I just had a little procedure.

15:06.939 --> 15:08.236
What kind of procedure?

15:08.407 --> 15:12.002
They sucked some fat out of her ass
and shot it into her lips.

15:14.813 --> 15:17.680
What did they do, use the whole ass?

15:19.918 --> 15:21.351
They're just a little swollen.

15:21.520 --> 15:24.353
In two days, they'll be plump,
luscious and ready for action.

15:26.225 --> 15:29.251
What boy doesn't like hearing that
from his mother?

15:29.628 --> 15:32.096
Charlie, I need to sit down.

15:32.264 --> 15:33.595
Got you covered.

15:33.766 --> 15:36.257
I thought... I thought you said
it was a woman thing.

15:36.435 --> 15:39.370
Do you know any guys
dumb enough to do this?

15:40.739 --> 15:42.331
Good Lord.

15:42.508 --> 15:44.601
What did you do, fellate a beehive?

15:46.912 --> 15:47.936
Fellate?

15:48.280 --> 15:51.010
I read. I can conjugate.

15:52.017 --> 15:56.579
Man, the last time I saw a mouth like that,
it was trying to eat Jacques Cousteau.

16:03.862 --> 16:05.124
Here you go, Mom.

16:05.297 --> 16:07.788
- Nice bite-size pieces.
- Thank you, darling.

16:08.734 --> 16:11.396
Dad says you got your butt in your lips.

16:17.276 --> 16:19.506
- Just eat your dinner.
- Hang on.

16:19.678 --> 16:22.613
So if you burped now,
it'd really be a fart, right?

16:28.320 --> 16:29.981
Eat.

16:32.091 --> 16:35.185
Charlie, my doughnut's too soft.

16:37.563 --> 16:40.999
So, Jake, has your mother succeeded
in turning you against me yet?

16:41.400 --> 16:42.628
Mom.

16:42.801 --> 16:44.769
What? You don't think she talks?

16:44.937 --> 16:46.336
You don't think he listens?

16:46.505 --> 16:48.939
Trust me, Alan,
even the mind of a dull child...

16:49.108 --> 16:51.372
...can be poisoned by a malicious parent.

16:51.810 --> 16:53.607
Can we just please change the subject?

16:53.779 --> 16:56.407
Although I must say,
I prefer your mother...

16:56.582 --> 17:00.040
...to that post-pubescent knucklehead
your father replaced her with.

17:00.486 --> 17:01.976
Okay. Okay, that's it.

17:02.154 --> 17:04.782
- I changed the subject.
- Jake, we're going to the movies.

17:04.957 --> 17:07.448
- On a school night?
- Why not? You're flunking anyway.

17:08.293 --> 17:10.124
Wait, wait, you're just leaving me?

17:10.295 --> 17:12.126
You're taking care of Mom, remember?

17:12.464 --> 17:13.488
That's not fair.

17:13.665 --> 17:16.156
You got a complaint,
take it to the floating head.

17:22.741 --> 17:25.209
- So how's work?
- Fine.

17:25.477 --> 17:26.842
You seeing anybody special?

17:27.379 --> 17:28.403
Nope.

17:29.748 --> 17:34.344
Charlie, did you ever stop to think
that our relationship is strained...

17:34.520 --> 17:37.353
...because you won't let me in,
you won't share?

17:37.823 --> 17:39.757
You know why I won't share
with you, Mom?

17:39.925 --> 17:42.086
Because anything I say
will be used against me.

17:42.261 --> 17:44.354
- Oh, please.
- I have to go to the bathroom...

17:44.530 --> 17:46.327
...maybe I have a prostate problem.

17:46.498 --> 17:49.558
I buy a new Mercedes,
you call it a Nazi phallic symbol.

17:50.836 --> 17:55.535
I'm seeing someone new, you ask
if I'm paying her by the hour or per schtup.

17:56.041 --> 17:59.101
Charlie, when I say those things,
it's because I want to help you.

17:59.278 --> 18:02.338
You're my son.
I want you to be the best you can be.

18:02.981 --> 18:05.449
I appreciate that,
but you can stop worrying.

18:05.617 --> 18:06.709
I'm doing fine.

18:06.885 --> 18:08.853
I am the best I can be.

18:09.655 --> 18:12.749
Oh, darling, that just breaks my heart.

18:22.367 --> 18:24.392
Why would he do this to me?

18:24.570 --> 18:27.004
"Take care of your mother. "

18:27.172 --> 18:29.299
Not like she ever took care of him.

18:29.474 --> 18:34.173
She nagged him, humiliated him,
emasculated him.

18:34.346 --> 18:38.146
Main reason he died so young
is because he wanted to.

18:38.684 --> 18:42.176
EvELYN:
Charlie, my doughnut's soft again.

18:42.354 --> 18:44.481
Be right there.

18:45.357 --> 18:46.415
Why?

18:46.592 --> 18:48.856
Why do you want me
to take care of her?

18:49.027 --> 18:50.892
EvELYN:
Charlie.

18:51.496 --> 18:53.020
I'm coming.

18:53.198 --> 18:54.631
Come on, talk to me.

18:54.800 --> 18:56.495
Give me a sign.

18:56.668 --> 19:00.900
RoSE
Marry that cute girl down the beach.

19:01.974 --> 19:02.963
Rose.

19:03.141 --> 19:06.133
RoSE
Yes, that's her name.

19:07.613 --> 19:09.740
You know what?
You can tell me in person...

19:09.915 --> 19:13.749
...because I am this close
to sticking my tongue in a light socket.

19:14.519 --> 19:17.647
RoSE Why don't you
stick your tongue in my mouth instead?

19:18.457 --> 19:22.120
RoSE
I mean, Rose's mouth.

19:26.498 --> 19:27.760
Yeah, boss?&lt;/i>

19:27.933 --> 19:30.163
Shut the door and sit down.&lt;/i>

19:30.969 --> 19:33.767
- What are you watching?
- Some old gangster movie.

19:33.939 --> 19:36.407
I think she's gonna sing like a bird.&lt;/i>

19:36.708 --> 19:38.198
Any good?

19:38.377 --> 19:39.435
Not really.

19:40.279 --> 19:42.247
It just gives me a warm feeling
to know...

19:42.414 --> 19:46.316
...that all those young,
beautiful actors are now dead.

19:48.053 --> 19:49.850
The dame knows too much.&lt;/i>

19:50.022 --> 19:52.718
You want I should take care of her, boss?&lt;/i>

19:57.129 --> 19:59.359
Yeah, take care of her.&lt;/i>

19:59.531 --> 20:01.999
&lt;i>But make it look like an accident.&lt;/i>

20:04.303 --> 20:05.895
Don't worry about a thing.&lt;/i>

20:06.071 --> 20:08.266
&lt;i>I'll take care of her.&lt;/i>

20:09.341 --> 20:12.435
Sorry, I misunderstood.

20:14.813 --> 20:16.610
What's that, dear?

20:17.215 --> 20:18.239
Nothing.

20:32.798 --> 20:33.822
Hi.

20:34.833 --> 20:35.891
Hello.

20:36.868 --> 20:39.302
I don't know if you remember me.
I pulled you out...

20:39.471 --> 20:42.338
...of the ocean the other day.
- Oh, right, right, right.

20:42.507 --> 20:44.737
- Thanks.
- It's okay. It's my job.

20:44.910 --> 20:47.140
Well, I'm glad you did it.

20:47.312 --> 20:49.405
I was just checking in,
see how you're doing.

20:50.148 --> 20:52.912
- I'm doing fine.
- Good.

20:53.618 --> 20:59.318
So you wanna walk down to the pier,
maybe grab a cup of coffee?

21:07.332 --> 21:09.391
Gee, uh, I don't know.

21:09.568 --> 21:10.933
EvELYN:
Charlie.

21:11.103 --> 21:14.266
It's time to change my butt dressing.

21:16.675 --> 21:18.540
Ah, what the hell, let's go.
